/site/asset-backups/

# Local agent workspace. DEFAULT = PRIVATE: everything under .claude/ stays local
# (wallet-audit outputs with test-wallet addresses+balances, third-party outreach
# contacts, internal strategy/plans, ~294MB of node_modules, settings, the README index).
# We ship ONLY an explicit allowlist of audited, contributor-facing material below.
# To publish a NEW skill `foo`: add `!/.claude/skills/foo/`. See .claude/README.md.
# (CLAUDE.md is committed as the public project guide; AGENTS.md is the agent-facing one.)
/.claude/*
!/.claude/commands/
!/.claude/skills/
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/add-chain-integration/
!/.claude/skills/site-design/
!/.claude/skills/release/
!/.claude/skills/verify-gate/
!/.claude/skills/deploy/

# Stray local screenshots
screencapture-*.png
Screenshot*.png

# Research & design notes now live under /.claude/ (already ignored above) — local only.

# === Design skill (.claude/skills/site-design/design/) — STRICT source-vs-render rule ===
# Every file is exactly one of: SOURCE (templates *.html, scripts *.mjs/*.py, docs *.md —
# TRACKED), PUBLISHED (brand/ + source/ — TRACKED, incl. their PNGs), or RENDER (anything a
# pipeline generates — IGNORED). The pipelines live under social/ and video/, so their
# generated PNG/MP4/audio, the assets.js bundle, and frame/sample dumps are kept out of git
# (regenerate them with the render scripts). The full rule is documented in design/README.md.
.claude/skills/site-design/design/social/**/*.png
.claude/skills/site-design/design/social/**/*.mp4
# chain-cards/ render.mjs writes a debug <chain>.html beside each <chain>.png — both are
# RENDER output here (the template is a string inside render.mjs), so ignore the HTML too.
# (post-cards/ and launch-cards/ .html ARE source templates, so this is scoped to chain-cards.)
.claude/skills/site-design/design/social/chain-cards/*.html
.claude/skills/site-design/design/video/**/*.png
.claude/skills/site-design/design/video/**/*.mp4
.claude/skills/site-design/design/video/**/*.wav
.claude/skills/site-design/design/video/**/*.mp3
.claude/skills/site-design/design/video/assets.js
.claude/skills/site-design/design/**/frames/
.claude/skills/site-design/design/**/sample/
.claude/skills/site-design/design/**/__pycache__/
